= Pressures =

Pressures are recorded in varying ways, depending on the machine model:

{| class="wikitable"
! Channel !! Models !! Description
|-
| Pressure Set || F0 || For single-pressure therapy, this is the target pressure, reported as individual events, which are linearly interpolated. For CPAP, this results an event at t=0 and an event at t=end, both with the prescribed pressure. For Auto-CPAP, this results in an event at t=0 with the starting pressure, then another event with the same pressure at t=X, and the next target pressure at t=Y, resulting in a linearly increasing (or decreasing) pressure between times X and Y, with subsequent events following the same pattern.
|-
| IPAP Set || F0 || For bi-level therapy, this is the target IPAP, reported as individual events along with EPAP Set (see below), which are linearly interpolated. See Pressure Set above for more detail.
|-
| EPAP Set || F0, F5 || For bi-level and autoSV therapy, this is the target EPAP, reported as individual events, which are linearly interpolated. See Pressure Set above for more detail.
|-
| Pressure&nbsp;Average || F0V4 and higher || A periodic statistic indicating the average pressure for the preceding 2 minutes. For bi-level therapy, this appears to be a true average, sitting between EPAP and IPAP. For single-level therapy, it is unclear whether this is the average pressure or the average effective EPAP when a Flex mode is enabled.
|-
| EPAP Average || F5, F3 || A periodic statistic indicating the average EPAP for the preceding 2 minutes.
|-
| IPAP Average || F5, F3 || A periodic statistic indicating the average IPAP for the preceding 2 minutes.
|-
| IPAP High || F5 || A periodic statistic indicating the maximum IPAP in the preceding 2 minutes.
|-
| IPAP Low || F5 || A periodic statistic indicating the minimum IPAP in the preceding 2 minutes.
|-
| Opti-Start Pressure || F0V4 and higher || (Tentative) An occasional individual event that appears to indicate a change in the Opti-Start pressure for future sessions. (Not currently imported)
|}


= Events =

{| class="wikitable"
! Channel !! Models !! Description
|-
| Pressure Pulse || F0, F5V3 and higher, F3V6 and higher || An individual event indicating a pressure pulse used by the machine to distinguish between OA and CA events. The meaning of its data value is currently unknown.
|-
|rowspan=2| Obstructive Apnea (OA)
| F0, F5, F3V6 || An individual event indicating an obstructive apnea event. No duration is reported.
|-
| F3V3 || A periodic statistic indicating the total number of obstructive apnea events in the preceding 2 minutes. These are currently imported as individual evenly spaced events across the 2-minute interval.
|-
|rowspan=2| Clear Airway Apnea (CA)
| F0, F5, F3V6 || An individual event indicating an clear airway apnea event. No duration is reported.
|-
| F3V3 || A periodic statistic indicating the total number of clear airway apnea events in the preceding 2 minutes. These are currently imported as individual evenly spaced events across the 2-minute interval.
|-
|rowspan=2| Hypopnea (H)
| F0, F5, F3V6 || An individual event indicating a hypopnea event. No duration is reported. Some machines (F0V2346) report multiple variations of HY whose distinctions are unknown. Some of them include additional unknown data.
|-
| F3V3 || A periodic statistic indicating the total number of hypopnea events in the preceding 2 minutes. These are currently imported as individual evenly spaced events across the 2-minute interval.
|-
| Flow Limitation (FL) || F0, F5 || An individual event indicating an flow limitation event. No duration is reported.
|-
| RERA (RE) || F0, F3V6 ||  An individual event indicating an respiratory-related arousal. No duration is reported.
|-
| Vibratory Snore (VS) || F0, F5 || An individual event indicating a vibratory snore event, drawn on official waveform reports. No duration is reported. This is currently imported as "VS2" to distinguish from the VS statistic (see below).
|-
| Timed Breath (TB) || F5, F3V6 || An individual event indicating the machine initiated a timed breath. The duration is reported in 100ms units.
|-
| Periodic Breathing (PB) || F0, F5, F3V6 || An individual event indicating a span of time during which periodic breathing was detected.
|-
| Large Leak (LL) || F0, F5, F3V6 || An individual event indicating a span of time during which a large leak was detected.
|-
| PRS1_0E (??)  || F0 only || An individual event indicating a span of time during which some unknown characteristic was detected.
|-
| Apnea Alarm || F3V6 only || An individual event indicating an apnea alarm at that time.
|-
| Pressure Set<br/> IPAP Set<br/>EPAP Set || F0<br/>F0<br/>F0, F5 || See Pressures table above.
|}

= Statistics =
Most statistics are reported every 2 minutes, summarizing the preceding 2 minutes (or less, at the end of a session or slice).

{| class="wikitable"
! Channel !! Models !! Description
|-
| Total Leak || F0, F5, F3 || A periodic statistic indicating the average(?) total leak for the preceding 2 minutes.
|-
| Unintentional Leak || F5V1 and higher, F3 || A periodic statistic indicating the average unintentional leak for the preceding 2 minutes.
|-
| Snore Count (VS) || F0, F5, F3V6 || A periodic statistic indicating the total number of vibratory snores in the preceding 2 minutes. These are drawn as flags in the detailed overview, but not on official waveform reports.
|-
| Respiratory Rate (RR) || F5, F3 || A periodic statistic indicating the average breath rate (BPM) for the preceding 2 minutes, reported as an integer.
|-
| Patient-Triggered Breaths (PTB) || F5, F3 || A periodic statistic indicating the percentage of patient-triggered breaths in the preceding 2 minutes.
|-
| Minute Ventilation (MV) || F5, F3 || A periodic statistic indicating the average minute ventilation for the preceding 2 minutes.
|-
| Tidal Volume (TV) || F5, F3 || A periodic statistic indicating the average tidal volume for the preceding 2 minutes.
|-
| Peak Flow Rate || F3V3 only || A periodic statistic indicating the peak flow rate in the preceding 2 minutes. Only needed in F3V3 as it does not report a flow waveform.
|-
| Test 1 || F3V6 only || A periodic statistic of unknown significance.
|-
| Test 2 || F3V6 only || A periodic statistic of unknown significance.
|-
| Snores at Pressure || F0 || An end-of-session series of statistics dividing the total snore count based on the target pressure (single or IPAP and EPAP) when they occurred. (Not currently imported)
|-
| Pressure Average<br/>EPAP Average<br/>IPAP Average<br/>IPAP High<br/>IPAP Low || F0V4+<br/>F5, F3<br/>F5, F3<br/>F5<br/>F5  || See Pressures table above.
|}